<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.7.1: Patterns in Real Numbers</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01366</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.7.1: Patterns in Real Numbers</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ae2b4d51-ef57-4c57-bc4e-795614463d3b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">In the table, find as many patterns as you can. Use one or more patterns
        to help you complete the table. Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>

      <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="6">
<tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>fraction</emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>32</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>decimal</emphasis></entry>
              <entry> 0.5 </entry>
              <entry> 0.25 </entry>
              <entry> 0.125 </entry>
              <entry> a._____ </entry>
              <entry> b._____ </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->

        <exercise id="cb38133c-fc76-4a75-bb30-617cc34e630d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">What is the value for a?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00003">Correct! 0.0625</para>
            <para id="para-00004">The correct answer is: 0.0625</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_5873a187-8e12-472a-bba2-e3dc88a7f04d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00005">What is the value for b?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00006">Correct! 0.03125</para>
            <para id="para-00007">The correct answer is: 0.03125</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
<!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00008">Describe the pattern you used to find the values that completed the
            table.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">


          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answers:</para>

          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>Each number is half of the previous number. We can find the next number by
              multiplying the current number by <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              or by 0.5, or by dividing by 2.</item>
            <item>The non-zero digits of the decimals are powers of 5 (<m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              , <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              , <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>,
              etc.), and each time there is an additional decimal place.</item>
            <item>0.5 can be written as <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>,
              0.25 as <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>25</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>100</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>,
              and 0.125 as <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>125</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>000</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.
              The numerators are powers of 5, and the denominators are powers of 10, so the next two
              numbers are <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>,
              which is <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>65</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                      <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>000</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              or 0.0625, and <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>,
              which is <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>125</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>100</m:mn>
                      <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>000</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              or 0.03125.</item>
            <item>The denominators in the fractions are powers of 2.</item>
          </list>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>